# AOSP does not map /data/nfc, and the files inside inherit system_data_file.
# With this line they get the type they deserve, and the fallback rule in
# nfc.te can go once every device has been relabelled.
/data/nfc(/.*)?    u:object_r:nfc_data_file:s0


# The fstab at the root of system, the one vold reads.
#
# AOSP labels any /fstab.* as rootfs
# (system/sepolicy/private/file_contexts:9), and nobody may read rootfs:file
# unless explicitly allowed: modprobe, ueventd, vendor_init, update_engine.
# Not vold. With that type it could not open the file and would fall back to
# the vendor fstab, which is the problem we started from (see device.mk, above
# PRODUCT_COPY_FILES).
#
# This line is more specific than "/fstab\..*" and beats the generic match.
# Every domain can read system_file: system/sepolicy/public/domain.te says
# allow domain system_file_type:file { getattr open read map execute }.
/fstab\.s88pro    u:object_r:system_file:s0

# The EAS boost applier. It is executed directly rather than through
# /system/bin/sh, because init will not start a service that has no domain
# transition -- see sepolicy/system_ext/private/s88pro_schedtune.te -- and the
# transition is computed from the label of the file named in the service.
/system/bin/s88pro-schedtune\.sh    u:object_r:s88pro_schedtune_exec:s0

# The AIDL vibrator HAL. Same reason as the line above: init computes the
# domain transition from the label of the file it is told to execute.
# The alternation is not decoration. system_ext is a partition of its own on
# some devices and a directory inside system on others -- here it is the
# second, and /system_ext is a symlink to /system/system_ext. The image is
# labelled by physical path, so a rule matching only /system_ext never fires
# and the generic /(system_ext|system/system_ext)(/.*)? -> system_file wins.
# The binary then has no domain transition from init, init refuses to start
# the service without saying so on any channel that survives, and -- because
# the HAL is declared in VINTF -- the framework waits for it forever on
# AServiceManager_waitForService. That is a phone stuck on the boot animation.
# AOSP writes every system_ext rule this way; see plat_file_contexts.
/(system_ext|system/system_ext)/bin/hw/android\.hardware\.vibrator-service\.s88pro    u:object_r:hal_vibrator_s88pro_exec:s0
